## 3.1 Document Information

### Purpose

The Document Information section records the repository and document management metadata associated with a System Objective.

Its purpose is to uniquely identify the objective document as an engineering artifact and support governance, version control, and traceability.

---

### Standard Fields

Every System Objective document shall include the following fields:

| Field | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| Document Title | Official title of the objective document. |
| Document Identifier | Unique identifier for the document. |
| Objective Identifier | Permanent identifier of the System Objective (e.g., SO-F-001). |
| Objective Category | Approved objective category. |
| Document Status | Current lifecycle status of the document. |
| Version | Current approved document version. |
| Repository | Repository in which the document is maintained. |
| Parent Domain | System Objective Specification (SOS). |
| Parent Folder | Engineering category folder containing the objective. |
| Owner | Responsible governance role. |
| Approval Authority | Authority responsible for approval. |
| Effective Date | Date on which the current version becomes effective. |
| Last Updated | Date of the latest approved revision. |

---

### Requirements

The Document Information section shall appear at the beginning of every System Objective document.

Repository metadata shall remain consistent with the governance and version control standards established for AVIA.
